  "notes": "The 2017+ female-rap chart standard, and the rare entry on this axis with a full mix teardown behind it. Ultra-minimal by construction: one synth line, no pad, no bass instrument besides the 808 — so the harmony is a monophonic minor-pentatonic riff over a tonic sub. ⛔ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set because the flagship production is *famously chord-less*, and the riff is therefore the only thing stating a key. The chord part still generates so the tab is not empty, and its variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` [4,16], three `harmonicRhythm` values and a 34-semitone voicing register rather than from families the record does not contain. ⚠ `melody.register` starts at 74 on purpose: the Sound on Sound account says the vocal fills the mid-range and there is no melodic pad, so the synth stays above it. `monophonicBias` 0.85 is the \"main plus a variable second layer\" — mostly one line, occasionally two. ⚠ The three parallel 808 tracks — one transient-shaped, bass-enhanced and distorted so it \"almost functions like a bass\" — are one `bass808` block here with `distortion: heavy`; the engine has one sub voice, so the parallel processing is a mix fact this model cannot state. Likewise the three separately-EQ'd hat tracks read as one dense hat lane at `fillDensity` 0.7. ⚠ Rolls are used as fills rather than as texture, which is why `rolls.freqPerBar` is 0.18 — the low end of this author's band. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
